/ file.read with a Type lands that type itself (decision 831): `read notes.md as text` births the
/ content as a text, not a {file, md} reference. No `write to` here, so no capturing variable.set
/ can convert what the read landed — the read's own answer (%!data%) is what is checked.
/ AsTextKeepsText can't see this: its capture carries Type=text and converts a file reference too.
AsTextLandsTextUncaptured
- read notes.md as text
- assert.equals(Expected="text", Actual=%!data!type.name%, Message="the read itself lands a text, not a file reference")
